# Restart, data impact and restore boundary

Native6 is defined and requested but not executed at packet preparation. Resume by reading
Main's exact current heavy authorization/owner, then follow the existing frozen NATIVE6
command/source pins and finite resource/cleanup rules only after an actual one-use start.
A prepared command or definition is not an allocation or execution. There is no additional
native case, provider call, browser, build or compiler permission implied by this packet.
After an actual run, preserve failures and exact cleanup/input evidence before reporting it;
retain the copied pre-run pins as historical definitions. Main owns final configured checks.

No DDL, service implementation, permissions, public API/error ID, read-classifier or
credential format is changed. The Slack boundary now accepts only explicit revocation
confirmation or existing explicit unusable-current-token errors. The existing service
remains responsible for pending/local blocking, encrypted retry material, clearing on
accepted confirmation and the disconnected audit event. Unit evidence does not yet prove
those PostgreSQL outcomes; the six-case native selection is still unexecuted.

Main records its actual current preimages and reconciles the four paths. The registry
postimage is exact a7-plus-one-digest reference context, not permission to overwrite newer
Main metadata. Abandoning this unapplied packet changes no source/runtime state. If Main
later rolls back a landed change, revert only the bounded landed hunks while preserving
peer work, rerun required current checks, and retain the evidence. Do not reset/clean other
workspaces or replace the entire current registry with a historical file.

Restoring the older Slack parser can restore the false-confirmation defect. Code rollback
cannot reconstruct credentials previously cleared by a disconnect or prove upstream
revocation. Keep ambiguous outcomes explicit and use the existing reviewed OAuth reconnect
flow when new authorization is required; do not resurrect credential rows or infer an app
uninstall/all-token revoke from a local disconnected state. No installed database restore
or operational provider recovery is performed or qualified by this source packet.
